328
00:20:15.228 --> 00:20:18.988
Kia ora chair and committee. Thank you very much for inviting Tourism

329
00:20:19.448 --> 00:20:23.168
Industry Aotearoa to submit for you in person today.

330
00:20:23.228 --> 00:20:26.928
I am Rebecca Ingram, the chief executive of Tourism Industry Aotearoa.

331
00:20:27.508 --> 00:20:31.328
We have approximately 1,200 tourism businesses who are our members.

332
00:20:31.828 --> 00:20:35.788
That stretches from everything from Kapiti Island Nature Tours through

333
00:20:35.828 --> 00:20:36.808
to Air New Zealand.

334
00:20:37.888 --> 00:20:41.828
Tourism and conservation are deeply connected.

335
00:20:43.148 --> 00:20:47.128
New Zealand's natural environment is the foundation of many visitors'

336
00:20:47.268 --> 00:20:50.808
experiences, and tourism operators have a strong

337
00:20:50.928 --> 00:20:54.708
interest in tourism and conservation working well together,

338
00:20:55.188 --> 00:20:57.848
and conservation being protected and enhanced.

339
00:20:59.148 --> 00:21:02.468
Retaining the status quo is not our preferred option.

340
00:21:03.208 --> 00:21:05.848
We strongly support the direction of the reform.

341
00:21:06.748 --> 00:21:10.297
Our submission is about getting the system settings

342
00:21:10.528 --> 00:21:10.808
right.

343
00:21:12.108 --> 00:21:14.888
There are three areas I would like to focus on today.

344
00:21:16.368 --> 00:21:20.328
Our first concern is the proposed function requiring

345
00:21:20.338 --> 00:21:21.048
the department

346
00:21:21.948 --> 00:21:25.528
to enable use and development to the greatest extent.

347
00:21:27.088 --> 00:21:29.088
We think the wording in the bill goes too far.

348
00:21:31.088 --> 00:21:34.608
It potentially creates uncertainty about whether economic

349
00:21:34.648 --> 00:21:38.228
development is being elevated above conservation outcomes.

350
00:21:39.408 --> 00:21:43.268
Our preferred wording is simple. DOC should enable use and

351
00:21:43.328 --> 00:21:46.868
development to the extent consistent with conservation.

352
00:21:48.328 --> 00:21:52.228
Making this change will give DOC a clear and positive mandate to

353
00:21:52.268 --> 00:21:56.108
recognize and enable appropriate economic

354
00:21:56.118 --> 00:21:59.248
development and tourism opportunities while

355
00:21:59.288 --> 00:22:02.048
establishing a clear conservation boundary.

356
00:22:03.008 --> 00:22:06.288
This balance is something the legislation must strike.

357
00:22:09.108 --> 00:22:12.848
With regard to concessions and investment certainty, TIA

358
00:22:13.008 --> 00:22:16.248
strongly supports the intent of modernizing concessions.

359
00:22:16.908 --> 00:22:20.488
Our comments relate to concession system, both in terms

360
00:22:20.648 --> 00:22:24.628
of how the concessions are granted and how competitive allocation

361
00:22:24.648 --> 00:22:25.048
will work.

362
00:22:26.348 --> 00:22:30.268
For a tourism operator, a concession is often the cornerstone

363
00:22:30.308 --> 00:22:31.068
of their business.

364
00:22:32.708 --> 00:22:36.328
It allows them to invest in facilities, people and

365
00:22:36.368 --> 00:22:36.868
systems.

366
00:22:37.798 --> 00:22:41.538
Many concessionaires have spent decades developing

367
00:22:41.588 --> 00:22:45.568
operations around particular places, and are genuine

368
00:22:45.628 --> 00:22:48.748
partners in conservation efforts.

369
00:22:48.758 --> 00:22:52.298
They invest in predator control, restoration projects,

370
00:22:52.708 --> 00:22:56.538
visitor education, yet the current framework can feel

371
00:22:56.588 --> 00:22:58.488
more transactional than collaborative.

372
00:22:59.628 --> 00:23:03.568
Here is an example of how the current system can play out for a tourism

373
00:23:03.608 --> 00:23:04.058
business.

374
00:23:05.168 --> 00:23:08.488
We have a TIA member that has been operating

375
00:23:08.568 --> 00:23:11.588
responsibly on PCL for almost 40 years,

376
00:23:12.168 --> 00:23:15.748
including making a significant contribution to conservation.

377
00:23:17.008 --> 00:23:20.998
Following the process outlined by DOC, they applied to renew their concession when

378
00:23:21.028 --> 00:23:23.238
it was due to expire in 2023.

379
00:23:24.688 --> 00:23:28.048
DOC initially offered a concession that in some cases

380
00:23:28.208 --> 00:23:31.148
reduced their allocation by over 90%,

381
00:23:31.948 --> 00:23:33.728
completely devaluing their business.

382
00:23:35.508 --> 00:23:39.468
It then took two and a half years to prove

383
00:23:39.478 --> 00:23:42.888
their case, which highlighted inconsistencies in

384
00:23:42.948 --> 00:23:46.468
interpretation of planning documents, and the allocation of

385
00:23:46.508 --> 00:23:50.408
concessions to other operators. They were finally granted

386
00:23:50.418 --> 00:23:53.088
their satisfactory concession in June this year.

387
00:23:55.128 --> 00:23:58.068
While individuals within the department, and I want to make this clearly, were

388
00:23:58.188 --> 00:24:00.328
genuinely sympathetic and helpful,

389
00:24:01.628 --> 00:24:03.668
they were at the mercy of a broken system

390
00:24:04.828 --> 00:24:08.328
that was disempowering businesses and frustrating DOC.

391
00:24:10.008 --> 00:24:13.488
For this reason, gains around efficiency,

392
00:24:13.868 --> 00:24:17.588
statutory time frames, and improvements to granting

393
00:24:17.688 --> 00:24:19.868
processes are very much supported.

394
00:24:21.708 --> 00:24:25.568
With regard to competitive allocation, we acknowledge that competition may

395
00:24:25.648 --> 00:24:28.648
be entirely appropriate in some circumstances

396
00:24:29.600 --> 00:24:33.340
But operators need clarity about when competitive allocation might

397
00:24:33.480 --> 00:24:36.870
occur, how existing investment and conservation

398
00:24:36.960 --> 00:24:38.730
contributions will be recognised.

399
00:24:39.470 --> 00:24:43.150
That certainty is critical to continued investment and

400
00:24:43.200 --> 00:24:47.140
visitor experiences on conservation land, and we therefore ask

401
00:24:47.180 --> 00:24:51.000
the committee to recommend greater clarity in the bill around

402
00:24:51.060 --> 00:24:52.340
competitive allocation.

403
00:24:53.920 --> 00:24:57.120
We have similar feedback around pre-approved concessions.

404
00:24:57.840 --> 00:25:00.720
We support the principle. Removing unnecessary

405
00:25:00.740 --> 00:25:04.640
bureaucracy for straightforward, low impact activities does

406
00:25:04.680 --> 00:25:07.930
make sense, but the design needs appropriate safeguards.

407
00:25:08.940 --> 00:25:12.400
In particular, the 12 month approval may be too

408
00:25:12.460 --> 00:25:15.950
short to justify meaningful investment in

409
00:25:16.040 --> 00:25:19.780
staff, equipment, safety systems, and product quality.

410
00:25:20.889 --> 00:25:24.300
There's a risk that a mechanism designed to make the system easier

411
00:25:25.140 --> 00:25:28.620
could inadvertently favor short term, low investment

412
00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:31.610
operators over businesses committed to a place for a long

413
00:25:31.700 --> 00:25:35.660
time. There are also questions around cumulative effect,

414
00:25:35.980 --> 00:25:39.840
carrying capacity, and how pre-approved activities

415
00:25:39.900 --> 00:25:42.180
will interact with existing concessionaires.

416
00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:48.660
My third area of focus is the proposed international visitor access levy.

417
00:25:49.740 --> 00:25:53.610
Tia supports the principles, but our support comes with

418
00:25:53.640 --> 00:25:54.280
some conditions.

419
00:25:55.560 --> 00:25:59.480
First, the revenue should be additional to existing DOC funding.

420
00:25:59.520 --> 00:26:01.900
It should not simply substitute Crown funding.

421
00:26:01.980 --> 00:26:03.000
Oh.

422
00:26:03.160 --> 00:26:07.080
Second, we believe there should be a very strong connection between where

423
00:26:07.120 --> 00:26:09.640
the money is raised and the place that it's collected.

424
00:26:09.670 --> 00:26:09.810
Mm-hmm.

425
00:26:10.360 --> 00:26:14.120
So if a visitor is being charged for access to a place, they should be able to

426
00:26:14.220 --> 00:26:18.140
see their contribution improving conservation and the visitor experience

427
00:26:18.200 --> 00:26:18.550
at place.

428
00:26:19.440 --> 00:26:23.350
And third, implementation needs to consider how tourism is

429
00:26:23.380 --> 00:26:23.740
sold.

430
00:26:24.860 --> 00:26:28.840
Our submission therefore recommends at least 18 months notice before a

431
00:26:28.880 --> 00:26:32.780
new access charge takes effect, so operators can incorporate it

432
00:26:32.840 --> 00:26:36.480
into their pricing and international contracts if needed.

433
00:26:38.100 --> 00:26:41.820
We also need to consider the cumulative cost to the visitor rather than

434
00:26:41.860 --> 00:26:44.040
looking at each charge in isolation.

435
00:26:44.880 --> 00:26:48.840
An international visitor already pays, many of them, $100 in the international

436
00:26:48.900 --> 00:26:51.940
visitor levy. They may also face parking charges,

437
00:26:53.080 --> 00:26:55.380
and costs passed through from other concessionaires.

438
00:26:56.060 --> 00:26:59.520
An additional access charge needs to be considered as part of the

439
00:26:59.720 --> 00:27:01.400
overall visitor experience.

440
00:27:03.560 --> 00:27:03.980
Finally,

441
00:27:04.920 --> 00:27:05.400
excuse me.

442
00:27:06.280 --> 00:27:10.240
Many of the practical effects of this legislation will be determined by the policy

443
00:27:10.300 --> 00:27:13.540
statement, area plans, and visitor amenity areas, and

444
00:27:13.640 --> 00:27:15.600
through future regulations.

445
00:27:16.940 --> 00:27:20.740
We support tourism and recreation being explicitly recognized

446
00:27:20.780 --> 00:27:22.260
within the new planning framework.

447
00:27:23.480 --> 00:27:27.320
Not every operational detail should be in primary

448
00:27:27.400 --> 00:27:31.060
legislation, but Parliament does need to establish the important

449
00:27:31.160 --> 00:27:33.140
principles and guardrails now.

450
00:27:34.440 --> 00:27:38.020
We also think appropriate scrutiny and recommendation roles remain

451
00:27:38.140 --> 00:27:41.760
important, particularly given the greater concentration of

452
00:27:41.820 --> 00:27:44.720
decision making authority proposed within the bill.

453
00:27:47.280 --> 00:27:50.980
Tia strongly supports modernization of the conservation system.

454
00:27:51.500 --> 00:27:51.780
Mm-hmm.

455
00:27:51.860 --> 00:27:55.740
We want a system that's easier to navigate, provides certainty,

456
00:27:56.260 --> 00:27:58.320
encourages responsible investment,

457
00:27:59.220 --> 00:28:02.280
and enables tourism to contribute more to conservation.

458
00:28:03.820 --> 00:28:06.060
This bill should proceed with changes.

459
00:28:07.240 --> 00:28:10.820
Three things are fundamental. Conservation must remain the

460
00:28:10.900 --> 00:28:14.360
overriding purpose while enabling economic development.

461
00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:19.140
The concession system must provide sufficient certainty

462
00:28:19.560 --> 00:28:21.440
to encourage long-term investment,

463
00:28:22.320 --> 00:28:25.900
and the new powers, planning processes, and visitor charging

464
00:28:25.960 --> 00:28:28.920
mechanisms need some statutory guardrails.

465
00:28:30.600 --> 00:28:34.360
With those settings right, we believe this bill can

466
00:28:34.420 --> 00:28:37.820
deliver better outcomes for conservation, visitors,

467
00:28:38.300 --> 00:28:41.220
tourism businesses, and New Zealand. Thank you.

468
00:28:41.380 --> 00:28:42.400
I welcome your questions.

