also ask that Section 13E explicitly states that the National

738
00:43:18.336 --> 00:43:21.996
Conservation Policy Statement must classify outdoor education activities

739
00:43:22.076 --> 00:43:24.836
undertaken by not-for-profit providers as exempt.

740
00:43:25.316 --> 00:43:29.196
Those two things are required to give clarity and certainty.

741
00:43:30.256 --> 00:43:34.116
We also ask that Section 14A is broadened to make it really clear

742
00:43:34.136 --> 00:43:37.416
that cost recovery charges made by not-for-profit providers

743
00:43:37.796 --> 00:43:40.836
delivering education activities are not gain or reward.

744
00:43:41.376 --> 00:43:45.256
This would prevent these providers from being misclassified, as they

745
00:43:45.336 --> 00:43:49.216
currently are, as businesses simply because they charge to cover gear,

746
00:43:49.336 --> 00:43:50.896
staffing, and instructor costs.

747
00:43:52.096 --> 00:43:54.496
Relying on interpretation or ministerial

748
00:43:54.576 --> 00:43:57.856
discretion alone provides

749
00:43:57.896 --> 00:44:01.356
insufficient long-term certainty for the outdoor education sector.

750
00:44:01.916 --> 00:44:05.656
Clear statutory direction is needed to address this inequity and ensure

751
00:44:05.716 --> 00:44:09.496
young people continue to have opportunities to take part in outdoor

752
00:44:09.556 --> 00:44:13.236
education on public conservation land, regardless of who is running that

753
00:44:13.256 --> 00:44:13.856
activity.

754
00:44:15.376 --> 00:44:17.716
